          "nodes": [
            {
              "databaseId": 4254948595,
              "author": {
                "login": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer"
              },
              "body": "Empty supplied values collapse to a bare short option here. For example, `stash show` marks required `-I` and `-O` values as attached, so `[['-I', ''], ['-p']]` becomes `-I -p`; Git then treats `-p` as `-I`'s argument (or reports a missing argument), rather than preserving the empty regex and patch option. Reject empty values for required attached options in both runtime and literal validation (for example via option checks on the stash overrides) so accepted calls cannot be serialized into different argv semantics.",
              "url": "https://github.com/ash-r1/type-git/pull/135#discussion_r4254948595"
            },
            {
              "databaseId": 4255000127,
              "author": {
                "login": "ash-r1"
              },
              "body": "Fixed in 120945c. Native Git 2.55 confirms that `stash show -I \"\" -p` and `-O \"\" -p` treat the detached empty word as a stash reference and fail; attaching it would collapse the value boundary. Added source-backed nonempty checks to only those two stash short-option overrides, regenerated runtime/exploration artifacts, and added rejected public compiler fixtures. Valid `--ignore-matching-lines=` remains accepted and is covered by a native output comparison. Full source/contracts and six modern regression tests pass; Git 2.25 passes four tests with two documented version-specific skips. The native comparison now checks process errors, signals and status before comparing stdout.",
              "url": "https://github.com/ash-r1/type-git/pull/135#discussion_r4255000127"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  }
